WEBVTT

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.918
And for those of you
on the other side of the conversation,

00:01:00.942 --> 00:01:03.736
I have some advice for you too,
on how you can best listen,

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.096
respond and be an active ally
for your colleague.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.172
I can't give you the exact words to say,

00:01:08.196 --> 00:01:10.216
because they should be your own.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.964
After all I don't know
what you're keeping in your closet.

00:01:12.988 --> 00:01:14.187
But whatever it might be,

00:01:14.211 --> 00:01:16.609
I hope these tips
will provide you with a framework

00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:19.458
that's going to help you decide
exactly what you want to say

00:01:19.482 --> 00:01:20.776
and how you want to say it.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.536
Know what you want and don't want
out of the conversation.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.666
To know this, ask yourself questions like,

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:26.848
do I need anything

00:01:26.872 --> 00:01:28.927
from the person
that I'm disclosing this to?

00:01:28.951 --> 00:01:31.260
Where do I want the conversation
to go from here,